course: dictionary
lesson: 15203
title: Words for kind actions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone did something. Read the words around the new word to find its meaning. «Mia gave her last biscuit to her little brother, selflessly.» She gave away her last biscuit, so selflessly must describe a kind way of acting.
explain: «The nurses worked selflessly through the long night.» Think about who is working and why. Nurses help sick people, and they worked all night without stopping for themselves. So selflessly means thinking about others more than yourself.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «Sam gave his pocket money to build a new library and never asked for thanks.» He gave his money, and he did not want anything back. Selflessly means generously and without wanting a reward. Check it: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Selflessly» means in a way that thinks about others more than yourself.
fact: «Selflessly» also means generously, without wanting a reward.
fact: «Selflessly» tells you how someone does something, such as how a nurse works or how a friend gives.
fact: «Selflessly» is linked to the word selfless, which means without thinking about yourself first.
fact: In church, Christians believe Jesus loved selflessly, so the word is often used in stories and talks about faith.
exercise: «Mia gave her last biscuit to her little brother, selflessly.» What does selflessly mean? | Eating very fast | *Thinking of others more than herself | Asking for a reward | Hiding it from everyone
exercise: «The nurses worked selflessly through the long night.» Which word tells you how the nurses worked? | *selflessly | nurses | night | long
exercise: «Sam gave his pocket money to build a new library and never asked for thanks.» How did Sam act? | *Selflessly, to help others | Carelessly, and lost the money | Sadly, with a frown | Greedily, to get more for himself
test: «The hero ran into the burning house to rescue the cat, acting selflessly.» What does selflessly mean in this sentence? | Quickly, to win a prize | Without caring about anyone | Loudly and proudly, so everyone could see | *Generously, thinking of others before herself
test: Why would someone act selflessly? | To get a reward | *To help others, not for themselves | To be seen as the best | To avoid doing homework
exam: A friend says selflessly means selfishly. Which answer is right? | *No, selflessly means thinking about others, the opposite of selfishly | Yes, both mean greedy | It means lazily | Yes, they mean the same thing
